#### JSP Lifecycle

```
1. Translation Phase
   └─> JSP converted to Java servlet code
   └─> Filename: PageName_jsp.java
   
2. Compilation Phase
   └─> Java source compiled to bytecode (.class)
   └─> Filename: PageName_jsp.class
   
3. Instantiation Phase
   └─> Servlet instance created
   └─> Thread pool ready for requests
   
4. Initialization Phase
   └─> jspInit() method called once
   └─> Initialize resources
   
5. Request Processing Phase
   └─> _jspService() called for each request
   └─> Contains page logic and output
   
6. Destruction Phase
   └─> jspDestroy() called before unloading
   └─> Cleanup resources
```

#### Built-in JSP Objects (Implicit Objects)

| Object | Type | Scope | Description |
|--------|------|-------|-------------|
| request | HttpServletRequest | Page | Current HTTP request |
| response | HttpServletResponse | Page | HTTP response to send |
| session | HttpSession | Application | User session data |
| application | ServletContext | Application | Application-wide data |
| out | JspWriter | Page | Output stream to page |
| pageContext | PageContext | Page | Page context information |
| config | ServletConfig | Page | Servlet configuration |
| page | Object | Page | Current page instance (this) |
| exception | Throwable | Page | Uncaught exception (error page) |

