#### JSP Best Practices

```jsp
<!-- BAD: Too much logic in JSP -->
<%
    List<User> users = userDAO.findAll();
    for (int i = 0; i < users.size(); i++) {
        User user = users.get(i);
        if (user.isActive()) {
            out.println("<tr><td>" + user.getName() + "</td></tr>");
        }
    }
%>

<!-- GOOD: Use JSTL with EL -->
<c:forEach var="user" items="${users}">
    <c:if test="${user.active}">
        <tr><td>${user.name}</td></tr>
    </c:if>
</c:forEach>

<!-- BAD: Direct database access in JSP -->
<%
    Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:...");
    Statement stmt = conn.createStatement();
    ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery("SELECT * FROM users");
%>

<!-- GOOD: Use service layer -->
<%
    List<User> users = userService.getAllUsers();
    request.setAttribute("users", users);
%>
```

**Keypoints for JSP:**
- Combination of HTML and Java code
- Compiled to servlet at runtime
- Implicit objects available (request, response, session, etc.)
- JSP directives configure page behavior
- JSTL tags reduce scriptlet usage
- Expression Language (EL) simplifies variable access
- Lifecycle: translate → compile → instantiate → init → service → destroy
- Keep JSP focused on presentation, use services for logic
- Error pages for exception handling
- Caching directives improve performance

### 3. Filters

#### What are Filters?

Filters are components that intercept requests and responses in the servlet pipeline. They perform pre-processing before the request reaches the servlet and post-processing after the servlet generates a response.

#### Filter Architecture

```
Client Request
    ↓
Filter 1 (pre-processing)
    ↓
Filter 2 (pre-processing)
    ↓
Servlet
    ↓
Filter 2 (post-processing)
    ↓
Filter 1 (post-processing)
    ↓
Response to Client
```

#### Common Filter Use Cases

1. **Logging**: Log all HTTP requests and response times
2. **Authentication**: Verify user identity before accessing resources
3. **Authorization**: Check user permissions
4. **Compression**: Compress response for bandwidth optimization
5. **Caching**: Add cache control headers
6. **Character Encoding**: Ensure proper character encoding
7. **Error Handling**: Catch and handle exceptions
8. **Input Validation**: Validate request parameters
9. **CORS**: Handle cross-origin requests
10. **Request/Response Wrapper**: Modify request/response

#### Filter Interface

```java
public interface Filter {
    // Called once during initialization
    void init(FilterConfig filterConfig) throws ServletException;
    
    // Called for each request/response pair
    void doFilter(ServletRequest request, 
                 ServletResponse response, 
                 FilterChain chain) throws IOException, ServletException;
    
    // Called before container removes filter instance
    void destroy();
}
```

#### Filter Example

```java
@WebFilter(
    urlPatterns = {"/*"},
    filterName = "AuthenticationFilter",
    dispatcherTypes = {DispatcherType.REQUEST, DispatcherType.FORWARD}
)
public class AuthenticationFilter implements Filter {
    
    private static final Logger logger = 
        LoggerFactory.getLogger(AuthenticationFilter.class);
    
    @Override
    public void init(FilterConfig filterConfig) 
            throws ServletException {
        String excludePaths = filterConfig.getInitParameter("excludePaths");
        logger.info("AuthenticationFilter initialized. Exclude: " + excludePaths);
    }
    
    @Override
    public void doFilter(ServletRequest request, 
                        ServletResponse response, 
                        FilterChain chain) 
            throws IOException, ServletException {
        
        HttpServletRequest httpRequest = 
            (HttpServletRequest) request;
        HttpServletResponse httpResponse = 
            (HttpServletResponse) response;
        
        String uri = httpRequest.getRequestURI();
        logger.debug("Processing request: {}", uri);
        
        // Pre-processing
        String token = httpRequest.getHeader("Authorization");
        
        if (isPublicPath(uri)) {
            // Public paths don't need authentication
            chain.doFilter(request, response);
        } else if (token != null && isValidToken(token)) {
            // Token valid, proceed
            String username = extractUsername(token);
            httpRequest.setAttribute("authenticatedUser", username);
            chain.doFilter(request, response);
        } else {
            // Unauthorized
            logger.warn("Unauthorized access attempt to: {}", uri);
            httpResponse.setStatus(HttpServletResponse.SC_UNAUTHORIZED);
            httpResponse.getWriter().println("Unauthorized");
        }
        
        // Post-processing (response already generated)
        long contentLength = httpResponse.getContentLength();
        logger.debug("Response content length: {}", contentLength);
    }
    
    @Override
    public void destroy() {
        logger.info("AuthenticationFilter destroyed");
    }
    
    private boolean isPublicPath(String uri) {
        return uri.startsWith("/login") || uri.startsWith("/register");
    }
    
    private boolean isValidToken(String token) {
        return token != null && token.startsWith("Bearer ");
    }
    
    private String extractUsername(String token) {
        // Extract and verify JWT or session token
        return "user";
    }
}
```

#### Logging Filter

```java
@WebFilter(urlPatterns = "/*")
public class LoggingFilter implements Filter {
    
    private static final Logger logger = 
        LoggerFactory.getLogger(LoggingFilter.class);
    
    @Override
    public void doFilter(ServletRequest request, 
                        ServletResponse response, 
                        FilterChain chain) 
            throws IOException, ServletException {
        
        HttpServletRequest httpRequest = 
            (HttpServletRequest) request;
        long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        
        try {
            logger.info("{} {} - IP: {}", 
                httpRequest.getMethod(),
                httpRequest.getRequestURI(),
                httpRequest.getRemoteAddr()
            );
            
            chain.doFilter(request, response);
            
        } finally {
            long duration = System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime;
            HttpServletResponse httpResponse = 
                (HttpServletResponse) response;
            
            logger.info("Response: {} - Duration: {}ms",
                httpResponse.getStatus(),
                duration
            );
        }
    }
}
```

