**Singleton Session Beans**
- Single instance per application
- Shared across all clients
- Thread-safe access with proper synchronization
- Eager or lazy initialization
- Used for application-wide resources and caches

```java
@Singleton
@Startup // Initialize on application startup
@ConcurrencyManagement(ConcurrencyManagementType.CONTAINER)
public class ConfigurationService {
    
    private Properties config;
    private volatile long lastReload;
    
    @PostConstruct
    public void init() {
        loadConfiguration();
        lastReload = System.currentTimeMillis();
        System.out.println("Configuration service initialized");
    }
    
    @Lock(LockType.READ) // Multiple readers, no writers
    public String getProperty(String key) {
        return config.getProperty(key);
    }
    
    @Lock(LockType.WRITE) // Exclusive access
    public void setProperty(String key, String value) {
        config.setProperty(key, value);
    }
    
    @Lock(LockType.WRITE)
    public void reloadConfiguration() {
        loadConfiguration();
        lastReload = System.currentTimeMillis();
        System.out.println("Configuration reloaded");
    }
    
    private void loadConfiguration() {
        config = new Properties();
        // Load from file or database
    }
}
```

**Keypoints for Session Beans:**
- Encapsulate business logic and operations
- Stateless: pooled, scalable, lightweight (preferred for performance)
- Stateful: maintains state, one instance per client (use when needed)
- Singleton: application-wide resource, shared instance
- @PostConstruct, @PreDestroy lifecycle callbacks
- @TransactionAttribute controls transaction behavior
- Can be accessed locally or remotely
- Container manages pooling and lifecycle
- Lifecycle methods: init() → use → destroy()

#### 2. Message-Driven Beans (MDB)

**Theory:**
Message-Driven Beans (MDBs) are asynchronous components that consume messages from JMS queues or topics. They decouple message producers from consumers, enabling event-driven architectures.

```java
@MessageDriven(
    activationConfig = {
        @ActivationConfigProperty(
            propertyName = "destinationType",
            propertyValue = "javax.jms.Queue"
        ),
        @ActivationConfigProperty(
            propertyName = "destination",
            propertyValue = "java:/jms/queue/OrderQueue"
        ),
        @ActivationConfigProperty(
            propertyName = "messageSelector",
            propertyValue = "priority > 5"
        ),
        @ActivationConfigProperty(
            propertyName = "maxSession",
            propertyValue = "10"
        )
    }
)
public class OrderProcessorMDB implements MessageListener {
    
    private static final Logger logger = 
        LoggerFactory.getLogger(OrderProcessorMDB.class);
    
    @Inject
    private OrderService orderService;
    
    @Inject
    private EmailService emailService;
    
    @Override
    @TransactionAttribute(TransactionAttributeType.REQUIRED)
    public void onMessage(Message message) {
        try {
            if (message instanceof TextMessage) {
                TextMessage textMessage = (TextMessage) message;
                String orderJson = textMessage.getText();
                
                logger.info("Processing order: {}", orderJson);
                
                Order order = parseOrder(orderJson);
                orderService.processOrder(order);
                
                emailService.sendOrderConfirmation(order);
                
                logger.info("Order processed successfully");
                
            } else if (message instanceof MapMessage) {
                MapMessage mapMessage = (MapMessage) message;
                String orderId = mapMessage.getString("orderId");
                // Handle map message
            }
        } catch (JMSException e) {
            logger.error("Error processing message", e);
            // Message will be redelivered based on redelivery policy
        } catch (Exception e) {
            logger.error("Unexpected error", e);
        }
    }
    
