## Messaging Services (JMS) - Complete Guide

### What is JMS?

Java Messaging Service (JMS) is an API for creating, sending, and receiving messages asynchronously. It enables:
- Loose coupling between components
- Asynchronous communication
- Reliable message delivery
- Scalability through message brokers

### Messaging Models

#### 1. Point-to-Point (Queue Model)

```
Producer → Queue (Temporary Storage) → Consumer
- One message, one consumer
- Message persisted until consumed
- Consumer can process at its own pace
- No message lost if consumer temporarily unavailable
```

#### 2. Publish-Subscribe (Topic Model)

```
Publisher → Topic (Broadcast)
              ├→ Subscriber 1
              ├→ Subscriber 2
              └→ Subscriber 3
- One message, multiple subscribers
- Each subscriber gets copy
- Subscribers must be active to receive
- Dead subscribers miss messages (unless durable)
```

