16. **What is the difference between Container-Managed Transactions (CMT) and Bean-Managed Transactions (BMT)?**
    - **CMT (Container-Managed):**
      - Container handles transaction boundaries
      - Declarative via @TransactionAttribute
      - Simpler to implement
      - Better performance (less manual management)
      - Uses transaction attributes (REQUIRED, REQUIRES_NEW, etc.)
      - Recommended approach
    - **BMT (Bean-Managed):**
      - Application manages transaction explicitly
      - Manual begin/commit/rollback
      - More control but error-prone
      - Programmatic using UserTransaction
      - Can be less efficient due to manual overhead

