23. **How do you implement pagination efficiently in J2EE?**
    - **Pagination:** Retrieving subset of data
    - **Benefits:** Reduced memory, faster response, better UX

    ```java
    @Stateless
    public class ProductService {
        
        @Inject
        private EntityManager em;
        
        public PagedResult<Product> getProductsPaged(int pageNumber, int pageSize) {
            int offset = (pageNumber - 1) * pageSize;
            
            // Count total records
            long totalCount = (Long) em.createQuery(
                "SELECT COUNT(p) FROM Product p"
            ).getSingleResult();
            
            // Fetch page
            List<Product> products = em.createQuery(
                "SELECT p FROM Product p ORDER BY p.id",
                Product.class
            )
            .setFirstResult(offset)
            .setMaxResults(pageSize)
            .getResultList();
            
