## Common Design Patterns in J2EE

### 1. DAO (Data Access Object)
Separates persistence logic from business logic. Provides database-independent interface.

### 2. Service Locator
Centralizes lookup of services through JNDI (though dependency injection preferred now).

### 3. Session Facade
Session EJB provides simplified interface to complex entity relationships.

### 4. Model-View-Controller (MVC)
Servlet (Controller) → Service (Model) → JSP (View)

### 5. Observer
Event-driven architecture with JMS publishers and subscribers.

### 6. Factory
Factory methods for creating objects (e.g., JMSContext.createProducer()).

### 7. Interceptor
Aspect-oriented programming for cross-cutting concerns.

### 8. Dependency Injection
Container injects dependencies via @Inject annotation (preferred over lookup).

