## Common Mistakes and How to Avoid Them

### 1. Resource Leaks
❌ Bad:
```java
Connection conn = getConnection();
ResultSet rs = conn.getConnection().executeQuery(sql);
// No cleanup if exception occurs
```

✅ Good:
```java
try (Connection conn = getConnection();
     Statement stmt = conn.createStatement();
     ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(sql)) {
    // Auto-closed
}
```

### 2. N+1 Queries
❌ Bad:
```java
List<orders> = getOrders();
for (Order o : orders) {
    List<items> = o.getItems(); // One query per order!
}
```

✅ Good:
```java
List<orders> = em.createQuery(
    "SELECT o FROM Order o JOIN FETCH o.items"
).getResultList();
```

### 3. Missing Transaction Boundaries
❌ Bad: No transaction management
✅ Good: Use @Transactional or @TransactionAttribute

### 4. Hardcoded Dependencies
❌ Bad: `new UserDAO()`
✅ Good: `@Inject private UserDAO userDAO;`

### 5. Synchronous Processing of Heavy Operations
❌ Bad: Block servlet with long computation
✅ Good: Queue to JMS and process async

### 6. Ignoring Error Handling
